{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated executable -> game mappings (plans/GAME-SENSING-V2.md §2.4).",
    "",
    "This covers the HEAD of the play distribution, which is a different job",
    "from the tail. The Steam library scan resolves ~137k titles by",
    "install path with no per-game effort, but it only sees Steam installs.",
    "The most-played games on PC include League, Valorant, Fortnite,",
    "Hearthstone, WoW, Overwatch 2, Roblox and Genshin, none of which a Steam",
    "scan will ever find. Fifty hand-written lines buy all of them, on any",
    "launcher, on day one.",
    "",
    "FIELDS",
    "  game_id       Stable id used by the ledger, user_game_stats and the",
    "                spec-18 telemetry adapters. NEVER change one of these:",
    "                it is the key existing stats are stored under.",
    "  igdb_slug     Resolved at build time to an igdb_id plus display",
    "                metadata. May differ from game_id — IGDB calls Minecraft",
    "                'minecraft-java-edition', and splits StarCraft II across",
    "                three campaign entries.",
    "  exe           Executable basenames, matched case-insensitively.",
    "  path_contains Optional lowercase substring the full path must contain.",
    "                Required for shared runtime hosts: javaw.exe is Minecraft",
    "                only under a Minecraft install, and hl2.exe is several",
    "                different Valve games.",
    "",
    "Every row needs a human eye — IGDB's canonical names do not match",
    "intuition, and a wrong mapping silently attributes someone's session to",
    "the wrong game. Unresolved slugs fail the build loudly."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "mappings": [
